From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV=<n>: the descriptor update queues start at 1/n of their size and double on demand back to it; =1 counts only; a line every 3600 frames with the peak entries a frame and the grows; off by default

Port of part 1 of heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR #104 (branch perf/heap-memory, commit 0a5efdc,
docs/HEAP-MEMORY-RESEARCH.md), by heydemoura; his switch name kept. Read only, nothing run from it.

Our tree already has his shipping advice: 0107 made the queues a quarter of upstream's (guest
0x20000, compute 0x8000 entries a frame, 24 + 6 MiB host over 8 frames), so most of his 114 MiB is
in T173 already. This adds the small-start part on top: =8 starts guest at 0x4000 (3 MiB) and
compute at 0x1000 (768 KiB); his porch peak (76-80k guest, 12-14k compute a frame) would grow
guest back to 0x20000 and compute to 0x4000, so expect a few MiB, not 100.

Growth: our own path from 0535 (EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS), not Lichii #495's GrowDescriptorPayload.
In Acquire, before any entry is written: when used + reserve would not fit, double up to the
size the queue was built for (T173's), allocate the new array (bad_alloc caught: growth stops for
the session), WaitWorker, then swap. Past the ceiling or after a refusal the T173 path runs (wait
for the worker, start the frame's slice again). Every writer of both queues goes through Acquire
with its own reserve first (graphics ConfigureImpl and the fast delta draw incl. the L949 replay,
whose kept entries are a copied vector; compute pipeline Configure; the mesh-as-compute passes use
the draw's descriptor_data; every compute pass, FSR3 and the DLSS probe Acquire 2-3 or
resources.size()); the only readers of the array are scheduler.Record lambdas, which WaitWorker
drains before the old array goes. Both queues are used on the GPU thread only.

Off (unset, or not 1..64): exactly T173: same start sizes, same growth rule, no line.
=1: sizes and growth as without it, plus the lines (a control run's peak).
=2..64: start = max(size/n, 0x1000), grow to the T173 size at most.
Lines (Render_Vulkan): once per queue "EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV=<n> guest|compute queue: start
... ceiling ...", every 3600 frames "EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV guest|compute queue: 3600 frames:
peak N entries a frame, capacity ..., grows G, overflow waits W, refused R", and the existing
"Descriptor payload grew: a -> b entries" per grow.

vk_update_descriptor.cpp/.h only: not a translation id input (not under shader_recompiler and not
reached from it; not in SINGLE), no name in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.

---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp
index d383cff308b47ca9286c0b0878b2e2b35b4e1b09..62a77ff7d613919edfd3d374bbdba2c0c408169c 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
 
 #include <algorithm>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <new>
 #include <variant>
 #include <boost/container/static_vector.hpp>
@@ -19,20 +20,87 @@
 
 namespace Vulkan {
 
+namespace {
+// EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV=<n> (port of part 1 of heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR #104, branch
+// perf/heap-memory, commit 0a5efdc, by heydemoura; his switch name kept). Unset or not 1..64: off,
+// exactly T173 (no line, no growth). 1: sizes and growth as without it (T173), plus the count
+// line below, so a control run measures the peak. 2..64: each queue starts at 1/n of its T173 size (at least
+// 0x1000 entries a frame) and doubles on demand back to the T173 size at most; past that, or when
+// the larger array is refused, a full frame waits for the worker and starts again, as T173 does.
+// T173's sizes are already PR #104's shipping advice (0107: guest 0x20000, compute 0x8000).
+size_t StartDivisor() noexcept {
+    static const size_t divisor = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0') {
+            return size_t{0};
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const long parsed = std::strtol(value, &end, 10);
+        return (end != value && *end == '\0' && parsed >= 1 && parsed <= 64)
+                   ? static_cast<size_t>(parsed)
+                   : size_t{0};
+    }();
+    return divisor;
+}
+
+size_t StartPayloadSize(size_t size) noexcept {
+    const size_t divisor = StartDivisor();
+    if (divisor >= 2) {
+        return (std::max)(size / divisor, size_t{0x1000});
+    }
+    return Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS") ? size / 2 : size;
+}
+
+const char* QueueName(size_t full_size) noexcept {
+    return full_size == UpdateDescriptorQueue::GUEST_FRAME_PAYLOAD_SIZE     ? "guest"
+           : full_size == UpdateDescriptorQueue::COMPUTE_FRAME_PAYLOAD_SIZE ? "compute"
+                                                                            : "other";
+}
+} // Anonymous namespace
+
 UpdateDescriptorQueue::UpdateDescriptorQueue(const Device& device_, size_t frame_payload_size_,
                                              bool supports_descriptor_buffer_)
-    : device{device_}, frame_payload_size{Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS") ? frame_payload_size_ / 2 : frame_payload_size_},
+    : device{device_}, frame_payload_size{StartPayloadSize(frame_payload_size_)},
       supports_descriptor_buffer{supports_descriptor_buffer_},
       payload(std::make_unique_for_overwrite<DescriptorUpdateEntry[]>(frame_payload_size * FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT))
 {
     initial_frame_payload_size = frame_payload_size;
+    full_frame_payload_size = frame_payload_size_;
     payload_start = payload.get();
     payload_cursor = payload.get();
+    if (StartDivisor() != 0) {
+        LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                 "EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV={} {} queue: start {} entries a frame ({} KiB host), "
+                 "ceiling {} ({} KiB host)",
+                 StartDivisor(), QueueName(full_frame_payload_size), frame_payload_size,
+                 frame_payload_size * FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT * sizeof(DescriptorUpdateEntry) >> 10,
+                 full_frame_payload_size,
+                 full_frame_payload_size * FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT * sizeof(DescriptorUpdateEntry) >> 10);
+    }
 }
 
 UpdateDescriptorQueue::~UpdateDescriptorQueue() = default;
 
 void UpdateDescriptorQueue::TickFrame() {
+    if (StartDivisor() != 0) {
+        // EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV: the most entries one frame wrote (restarts included).
+        const size_t frame_entries = frame_entries_restarted +
+                                     static_cast<size_t>(std::distance(payload_start, payload_cursor));
+        frame_entries_restarted = 0;
+        peak_frame_entries = (std::max)(peak_frame_entries, frame_entries);
+        if (++ticks_since_report >= 3600) {
+            LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan,
+                     "EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV {} queue: 3600 frames: peak {} entries a frame, "
+                     "capacity {} (start {}, ceiling {}), host {} KiB, grows {}, overflow waits {}, "
+                     "refused {} (grows and waits since start)",
+                     QueueName(full_frame_payload_size), peak_frame_entries, frame_payload_size,
+                     initial_frame_payload_size, full_frame_payload_size,
+                     frame_payload_size * FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT * sizeof(DescriptorUpdateEntry) >> 10,
+                     grows, overflow_waits, growth_refused ? 1 : 0);
+            ticks_since_report = 0;
+            peak_frame_entries = 0;
+        }
+    }
     if (++frame_index >= FRAMES_IN_FLIGHT) {
         frame_index = 0;
     }
@@ -45,12 +113,14 @@ void UpdateDescriptorQueue::Acquire(Scheduler& scheduler, size_t required_entrie
     use_descriptor_buffer = supports_descriptor_buffer && use_descriptor_buffer_;
     static constexpr size_t DEFAULT_REQUIRED_ENTRIES = 0x400;
     const size_t reserve = required_entries > 0 ? required_entries : DEFAULT_REQUIRED_ENTRIES;
+    // EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV 2..64 grows the same way, to the T173 size at most.
+    static const bool start_div = StartDivisor() >= 2;
     static const bool trim = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS");
-    if (trim && !growth_refused) {
+    if ((trim || start_div) && !growth_refused) {
         const size_t used = static_cast<size_t>(std::distance(payload_start, payload_cursor));
         // EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS: grow back to 0107's size at most (2x the halved start), never
         // past it: a frame that needs more waits for the worker as before (below).
-        const size_t ceiling = initial_frame_payload_size * 2;
+        const size_t ceiling = start_div ? full_frame_payload_size : initial_frame_payload_size * 2;
         size_t grown = frame_payload_size;
         while (used + reserve >= grown && grown < ceiling) {
             grown = (std::min)(grown * 2, ceiling);
@@ -69,6 +139,8 @@ void UpdateDescriptorQueue::Acquire(Scheduler& scheduler, size_t required_entrie
                 scheduler.WaitWorker();
                 LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Descriptor payload grew: {} -> {} entries",
                          frame_payload_size, grown);
+                frame_entries_restarted += used;
+                ++grows;
                 payload = std::move(replacement);
                 frame_payload_size = grown;
                 payload_start = payload.get() + frame_index * frame_payload_size;
@@ -86,6 +158,8 @@ void UpdateDescriptorQueue::Acquire(Scheduler& scheduler, size_t required_entrie
         LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan, "Payload overflow (used={}, reserve={}, capacity={})",
                     used, reserve, frame_payload_size);
         scheduler.WaitWorker();
+        frame_entries_restarted += used;
+        ++overflow_waits;
         payload_cursor = payload_start;
     }
     upload_start = payload_cursor;
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.h
index 3623e6659902a13deb42687bcb00c0b24a849ba1..dd25fef9f3243ef4f6dbbf057b8d05b2816d61c5 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_update_descriptor.h
@@ -135,6 +135,14 @@ private:
     size_t frame_payload_size;
     size_t initial_frame_payload_size{}; ///< EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS: the start, after halving
     bool growth_refused{false};           ///< EDEN_UP_HEAP_HOLDERS: a growth was refused
+    // EDEN_DESCRIPTOR_START_DIV (heydemoura/EglantinePS5 PR #104, 0a5efdc): the size the queue
+    // was built for (the growth ceiling), and counts for its line every 3,600 frames.
+    size_t full_frame_payload_size{};
+    size_t frame_entries_restarted{}; ///< entries of this frame before a restart (grow or wait)
+    size_t peak_frame_entries{};
+    size_t grows{};
+    size_t overflow_waits{};
+    size_t ticks_since_report{};
     const bool supports_descriptor_buffer;
     bool use_descriptor_buffer{false};
     size_t frame_index{0};
